      timeline: [
        'Unknown: Traditional Draw dominoes establishes the core matching mechanic.',
        '1900s: Gambling variants like Auction emerge, adding chip pools to social games.',
        'Present: Popular in regions where dominoes remains a primary social competition.',
      ],
      evolution: 'The transition from score-based winning to pool-based winning allows for shorter, more intense rounds.',
      cultural: "Used as a 'session game' where players can drop in and out of the pool between rounds.",
    },
